        <tr><td>WA</td><td>$10,000</td><td>No</td><td>New homes, no stamp duty under $450K</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SA</td><td>$15,000</td><td>No</td><td>New builds, concessions for eligible buyers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>The cumulative impact of these grants and stamp duty differences can represent a <strong>$25,000 to $50,000 advantage for building</strong> compared to buying established — on top of any inherent price difference between the two options.</p>


